# Decision Modes

## Purpose

> **Scope:** The shared interaction-mode contract for {{skill-name}} procedures - how
> gates and decision points resolve in each mode.
> **Key items:** mode selection, resolution matrix, precedence, recording,
> reporting flags, permission boundary

Every procedure that offers a decision point resolves it through the modes
below, selected once at intake from the request's mode flag and carried through
the run.

## Mode Selection

- No mode wording selects `interactive` - the default.
- `autonomous`, `automatic`, `unattended`, `non-interactive`, `automated`, or
  `fully autonomous` wording selects the autonomous mode. {{skill-title}} keeps a single
  no-questions tier - `fully autonomous` resolves to the same `autonomous`
  mode, no stronger mode exists.
- `verbose`, `informational`, `diagnostic`, and `timing` are reporting flags
  that change what the operation emits, never what it decides or is permitted
  to do, per `process/json-exchange.md` and `process/operation-timing.md`.

## The Matrix

| Mode                  | Resolution                                            | Reporting                                                      |
|-----------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|
| `interactive`         | Present the options and ask at each decision point    | The offered options with the recommendation marked             |
| `autonomous`          | Resolve each decision point to the recommended option | Each resolution reported inline, never commits                 |
| `verbose`             | As the resolved mode requires                         | Every offered option plus the rationale for the recommendation |

## Resolution Precedence

A recommendation follows the same precedence everywhere: an explicit requester
choice first, then the target's own conventions, then verified evidence, then a
documented {{skill-name}} default.

A surface with no evidence stays unresolved rather than manufactured.

## Autonomous Recording

Every gate resolved under `autonomous` is reported inline at resolution time,
and the completion report carries a `Decisions:` list naming each resolved
surface and the option taken.

An unresolvable surface is reported rather than bypassed - {{skill-name}} has no mode
that suppresses reporting or skips a gate it cannot resolve.

## Reporting Flags

`verbose` modifies reporting only and never widens authorization - it composes
with the resolved mode, including interactive.

`informational` adds nothing beyond the timing paragraph, and `diagnostic` and
`timing` emit the parameter document of `process/json-exchange.md` for
information only.

## Permission Boundary

No mode grants permission to commit, delete, overwrite, or publish - those stay
separately gated in every mode.
